      "problem": "${3}^{-3}=\\frac{1}{27}$ can be expressed as",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={b}^{x}$ is equivalent to ${log}_{b}⁡a=x$\n\nIf we compare ${3}^{-3}=\\frac{1}{27}$ with $a={b}^{x},$ we get $a=\\frac{1}{27},b=3$ and $x=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation can be expressed as ${log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{1}{27})=-3.$",
